NAME
       curl - transfer a URL

SYNOPSIS
       curl [options] <url>

DESCRIPTION
       Fetches a URL and writes it to standard output by default. TLS
       1.3 is supported with certificate verification.

OPTIONS
       -X M   request method
       -d D   request body for POST (@file reads a file)
       -H H   add a header
       -A UA  set the User-Agent
       -e URL set the Referer
       -u U:P basic authentication
       -r R   request a byte range
       -L     follow redirects
       --max-redirs N   how many redirects to follow
       -i     include the response headers in the output
       -I     fetch headers only
       -D F   write the headers to F
       -o F   write the body to F
       -O     save under the name from the URL
       -k     do not verify the server certificate
       -s     silent
       -S     show errors even when silent
       -v     verbose
       -f     fail quietly on HTTP errors

EXAMPLES
       curl -s https://example.com/api | grep name
       curl -X POST -d '{"a":1}' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' URL

SEE ALSO
       wget(1), nc(1)
